kely either:\n1. A generic apiserver-level \"storage readiness\" gate (e.g. in staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/registry/generic/registry/store.go, or a dedicated storage_readiness.go / readiness.go file) that wraps Create/Update for resources whose backing informer/controller hasn't finished its initial sync (used for IPAddress and possibly ServiceCIDR, EndpointSlice, etc.)\n2. Somewhere that converts an internal error (e.g. ErrNotReady, or a \"not ready\" bool check) into a k8s.io/apimachinery apierrors.NewForbidden(...) call with that message.\n\nPlease locate:\n1. The exact file and function that constructs this \"not yet ready to handle request\" error string (grep-equivalent: search files under staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/registry/generic/registry/, staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/registry/rest/, and pkg/registry/core/rest/ and pkg/registry/networking/ for likely filenames like \"storage_readiness.go\", \"ready.go\", \"readiness.go\" \u2014 try reading them directly with read_file since ast_search appears broken for this repo (returns \"ast-grep failed\" for every language/pattern I've tried \u2014 don't rely on it, use read_file with guessed paths and list_files instead).\n2. How this readiness gate gets wired specifically to the IPAddress (and possibly ServiceCIDR) REST storage \u2014 i.e. where storage_core.go or the networking REST storage provider passes a \"ready\" check/hook into the generic Store (look for a field like `ReadyFunc`, `StorageReadiness`, or similar on genericregistry.Store, and where it's set for ipaddress storage).\n3. Confirm whether this ties to the same \"start-service-ip-repair-controllers\" PostStartHook / RepairIPAddress.RunUntil's onFirstSuccess callback, or to a separate readiness signal (e.g. the MetaAllocator's internal cache sync, or a dedicated post-start hook for the IPAddress/ServiceCIDR storage).\n\nReport back: the exact file path(s), the function/variable names involved, a short code excerpt showing where the strin